        "description": "Formulate as: compute per-model value v_j = r_j/s_j and size s_j. Aim to equalize the ratio across GPUs. Use scipy.optimize.linprog relaxation: variables x_{gj} in [0,1], constraints sum_g x_{gj}=1, sum_j s_j x_{gj} <= M - epsilon, minimize T s.t. sum_j (r_j/s_j) x_{gj} <= T*(M - sum_j s_j x_{gj}) for all g. Solve LP, then round fractional assignments greedily (assign each model to its highest-fraction GPU if memory allows, else best-fit), and finish with a repair pass.",
